  <h1>ASE-Lights Support</h1>

  <p>
    ASE-Lights helps users control WLED-compatible lighting devices on their local Wi-Fi network.
  </p>

  <h2>Contact Support</h2>

  <p>
    For support with ASE-Lights, please contact us at:
  </p>

  <p>
    <strong><a href="mailto:info@aselights.com">info@aselights.com</a></strong>
  </p>

  <p>
    When contacting support, please include your device type, iOS or Android version, app version,
    and a brief description of the issue you are experiencing.
  </p>

  <h2>Common Troubleshooting</h2>

  <h3>Device Discovery Issues</h3>

  <p>
    If ASE-Lights cannot find your WLED device, please try the following:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Ensure your phone and WLED controller are connected to the same Wi-Fi network.</li>
    <li>Ensure the WLED controller is powered on.</li>
    <li>Confirm that Local Network permission is enabled for ASE-Lights in your device settings.</li>
    <li>Restart the ASE-Lights app and try discovery again.</li>
    <li>Restart your WLED controller and router if the issue continues.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Unable to Control Lights</h3>

  <p>
    If your device is discovered but does not respond:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Confirm the WLED device is reachable on your local network.</li>
    <li>Check that the WLED device has a valid IP address.</li>
    <li>Make sure your phone is not connected to a guest network or VPN that blocks local devices.</li>
    <li>Try opening the WLED device directly in a web browser using its local IP address.</li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Presets or Schedules Not Updating</h3>

  <p>
    If presets or schedules are not updating correctly:
  </p>

  <ul>
    <li>Refresh the device in the app.</li>
    <li>Confirm the WLED device is online.</li>
    <li>Check that the preset exists on the WLED controller.</li>
    <li>Restart the app and try again.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>

  <p>
    You can view the ASE-Lights Privacy Policy here:
